docs {
  # Code Sets Registry Utility Service Tests
  
  Tests for the SIF 3.7 Code Sets Registry Utility Service endpoints.
  
  ## What Are Code Sets?
  
  Code Sets are a centralized registry of legal code values organized under named
  code sets. Consumers and providers use the registry to verify whether a received
  code value is legal, even if that value was not defined when the application was
  originally written. Code sets support zone-scoping: global entries can be
  overridden by zone-specific entries of the same name.
  
  ## URL Pattern
  
  Code set endpoints are scoped to a domain and solution:
  - `POST /{domainId}/{solutionId}/codeSets/codeSet` — Create a code set (admin only)
  - `GET /{domainId}/{solutionId}/codeSets` — List code sets (zone-scoped)
  - `GET /{domainId}/{solutionId}/codeSets/{id}` — Get code set by ID (zone-scoped)
  - `PUT /{domainId}/{solutionId}/codeSets/{id}` — Update code set (admin only)
  - `DELETE /{domainId}/{solutionId}/codeSets/{id}` — Delete code set (admin only)
  
  ## Tests Included
  
  - Create code set (admin, valid payload with codeItems and aliases)
  - List code sets (verify collection format)
  - Get code set by ID
  - Update code set (full replacement)
  - Delete code set
  - Create code set — non-admin rejected (403)
  - Zone scoping query — global + zone-specific override
  
  ## Prerequisites
  
  - A domain and solution must exist (createdDomainId, createdSolutionId)
  - A codeSets provider must be registered in the environment-global zone
  - Valid authentication credentials
  
  ## Important Notes
  
  - Code sets support full CRUD (unlike alerts which are immutable)
  - Only admin environments can create, update, or delete code sets
  - Any authenticated environment can query code sets
  - PUT does full replacement of the entire code set object
  - Zone-scoping: zone-specific entries override global entries with the same id
}
